delpezzo_char3_P2277_ninesing_verify_macmini_S171.py — verification record for

  X = X_14 = { x0^7 + x0^2 x1^5 + 2 x1^7 + x2^2 + x3^2 = 0 }  in  P(2,2,7,7)
  over F_3   (a(t) = t^7 + t^2 + 2 irreducible over F_3).

Checks (all PASS):
[1] P(2,2,7,7) well-formed (every weight triple coprime); weights prime to 3
    (tame; no wild quotient behavior in char 3).
[2] degree 14, Fano index sum(w) - d = 18 - 14 = 4 > 0; -K_X = O_X(4) ample.
[3] Structural decoupling: the 11 degree-14 monomials in these weights have NO
    mixed monomial (both blocks); F = A(x0,x1) + C(x2,x3) is forced.
[4] a(t) = t^7+t^2+2 irreducible/F_3 (trial division deg <= 3); gcd(a,a')=1
    (separable).  Quasi-smoothness: grad F = (A_0, A_1, 2x2, 2x3) = 0 forces
    x2=x3=0 and (Euler, 7=1 != 0 mod 3) A = A_0 = A_1 = 0, impossible for a
    separable form except at the irrelevant point; at (1:0), A_0 = 7 x0^6 != 0.
[5] Singular locus of X = exactly the ambient-strata points:
      * 7 geometric points {A=0} on the (2,2)-line, each 1/2(1,1) = A_1 (tame);
      * 2 geometric points {x2^2+x3^2=0} on the (7,7)-line (rational over F_9),
        each a 1/7(2,2) ~ 1/7(1,1) cyclic quotient point (tame, klt).
    TOTAL: 9 >= 8 singular geometric points; X is a klt del Pezzo surface.
[6] Exact point counts (value-distribution convolution over GF(3^k), k=1..4):
      q=3:  #X = 16   = q^2 + 2q + 1
      q=9:  #X = 82   = q^2 + 0q + 1
      q=27: #X = 784  = q^2 + 2q + 1
      q=81: #X = 6562 = q^2 + 0q + 1
    i.e. Tr(Frob^k | H^2(1)) = 2,0,2,0 — the exact signature of eigenvalues
    {1} ∪ {-zeta_7^j : j=1..6}:  1 + (-1)^(k+1) for 7 ∤ k.  Matches the lattice
    prediction below.

Picard rank (proof recorded in THM-2834):
  Geometrically, X contains 14 lines C_i = {A-root i, x2 = i*x3-type factor}
  over F_3bar: writing C = x2^2+x3^2 = (x2+ix3)(x2-ix3) = s·t, the divisors
  {s=0} and {t=0} split into 7 components each over the 7 roots of a.
  Intersection theory (H'^2 = 1/14, H'C_i = 1/14, C_i C_j = δ/2, C_i ≡ D_i
  numerically) gives NS(X_F3bar) ⊗ Q of rank 7 = b_2 (Noether: K_Xtilde^2 = -6,
  b2(Xtilde) = 16, minus 9 exceptional classes), spanned by H', C_1..C_7 with
  the single relation ΣC_i = 7H'.  Frobenius acts through the 7-cycle on the
  roots of the irreducible a composed with s <-> t (i in F_9 \ F_3):
  a single 14-orbit on {C_i, D_i}.  Invariants: Q·H' only.  Hence
      rho(X / F_3) = 1   (arithmetic Picard rank; Tate holds for geometrically
                          rational surfaces, and the point counts confirm),
      rho(X_F3bar) = 7   (geometric).
  Structural obstruction recorded: ANY quasismooth hypersurface in 4 weights
  whose >= 8 strata singularities include a (p,p)-line with >= d/2 points is
  forced decoupled (parity), hence contains the split lines and has geometric
  rho >= 2; and Method-A quotients of a SMOOTH CI(2,2) by a diagonal ±1
  involution have at most 4 singular points (signature (3,2) is forced;
  the P^1_- part of the fixed locus meets a smooth Y in 0 points because a
  common root of the two binary quadratics makes gradients parallel).  So 9
  points with arithmetic rank one is the honest optimum of this method family.

